---
title: Speech
sidebar:
  order: 2
---

To have an NPC say a message to the player, call `SpeakToPlayer` from an EVT script:

```c
Call(SpeakToPlayer, NPC_SELF, ANIM_Luigi_Talk, ANIM_Luigi_Idle, 0, MSG_CH0_0103)
```

The NPC turns to face the player, and the EVT script waits until the message closes.

These calls show messages in other ways:

| Call | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `SpeakToNpc` | Like `SpeakToPlayer`, but to another NPC |
| `ShowMessageAtScreenPos` | Shows a message that no one speaks, such as a sign, at a point on the screen |
| `ShowMessageAtWorldPos` | Shows a message that no one speaks at a point in the world |

## Keeping the box open

To do something between two messages without closing the box, end the first with `[Yield][End]` instead of `[Wait][End]`. The EVT script carries on while the box stays open. Then show the next message in the same box with `ContinueSpeech`, or close the box with `EndSpeech`:

```c
Call(SpeakToPlayer, NPC_SELF, ANIM_Goombaria_Talk, ANIM_Goombaria_Idle, 0, MSG_CH0_0098)
// ...
Call(ContinueSpeech, NPC_SELF, ANIM_Goombaria_Talk, ANIM_Goombaria_Idle, 0, MSG_CH0_009A)
```

A message that continues the box starts with `[Next]`.
